# Fixed 2026-10-01 by lane 135c (defect 141). Symptom: this file ends without
# a newline, and `check --apply` handed it back with one, a byte no fix
# proposed: on the compiler of `9d1c209d` it printed the file with `fn`
# repaired and a `\n` after `print(1)`, and `--in-place` wrote that into the
# file. Cause: `source.from_files` closed a file's open last line with a
# newline of its own, inside the file's text, which `--apply` hands back; and
# `cli/io.print_artifact` printed a text with no final newline through
# `print`, which adds one. Now the newline that joins two files belongs to
# neither, and an artifact is printed byte for byte. The `.fixed` is this
# text with `function` for `fn`, its last line open as here.

fn main()  #~ reserved_word
    print(1)